@startuml layers
' The layers of the receipt parser and what they use, see README.md in this package.
' Arrows point to what a layer uses. ReceiptLayout gets the checks of RowKinds passed in,
' so that it does not depend on it.

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName sans-serif
skinparam linetype ortho
top to bottom direction

[ReceiptParser\n<size:11>flow, total, discounts after it,\n<size:11>number of articles, merchant] as parser
[ReceiptAssembler\n<size:11>items from rows by named rules] as assembler
[RowKinds\n<size:11>what a row is, from its tokens] as kinds
[ReceiptLayout\n<size:11>rows from the positions of the lines,\n<size:11>tilt, price columns] as layout
[ReceiptTokens\n<size:11>numbers, units, signs, words;\n<size:11>the only place with regular expressions] as tokens
[ReceiptVocabulary.GERMAN\n<size:11>words of one language,\n<size:11>misread keywords] as vocabulary

parser --> layout
parser --> assembler
parser --> kinds
parser --> tokens
parser --> vocabulary
assembler --> kinds
assembler --> vocabulary
layout ..> kinds : passed in
kinds --> tokens
kinds --> vocabulary
tokens --> vocabulary

note right of layout
  Knows neither language
  nor recognition errors
end note

@enduml
